 463	% The source (references/qpbt-paper/06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:504-505) quantifies
 464	% the pairwise-agreement hypothesis over every pair (x, y_1), including pairs carrying
 465	% probability zero under D, on which no conditional distribution of y_2 is defined; the
 466	% hypothesis is restated here over the pairs of positive marginal probability, the only
 467	% pairs the sampling in the hypothesis can refer to and the only ones the averaged
 468	% conclusion depends on. The NEEXP original (references/neexp-paper/
 469	% 05_quantum_preliminaries.tex:1000-1008, label fact:low-degree-sandwich-on-steroids)
